# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "量子情報と量子計算に関する無料の IBM コース"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convex combinations of density matrices"
msgstr "密度行列の凸結合"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic selections of density matrices {#probabilistic-selections-of-density-matrices}"
msgstr "密度行列の確率的選択 {#probabilistic-selections-of-density-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A key aspect of density matrices is that *probabilistic selections* of quantum states are represented by *convex combinations* of their associated density matrices.\n"
msgstr "密度行列の重要な性質として、量子状態の*確率的選択*は、対応する密度行列の*凸結合*によって表されます。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, if we have two density matrices, $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$, representing quantum states of a system $\\mathsf{X}$, and we prepare the system in the state $\\rho$ with probability $p$ and $\\sigma$ with probability $1 - p$, then the resulting quantum state is represented by the density matrix\n"
msgstr "例えば、系 $\\mathsf{X}$ の量子状態を表す 2 つの密度行列 $\\rho$ と $\\sigma$ があり、系を確率 $p$ で状態 $\\rho$ に、確率 $1 - p$ で状態 $\\sigma$ に準備するとき、得られる量子状態は次の密度行列で表されます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p \\rho + (1 - p) \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p \\rho + (1 - p) \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, if we have $m$ quantum states represented by density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1}$, and a system is prepared in the state $\\rho_k$ with probability $p_k$ for some probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1})$, the resulting state is represented by the density matrix\n"
msgstr "より一般的には、密度行列 $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1}$ で表される $m$ 個の量子状態があり、確率ベクトル $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1})$ に従って確率 $p_k$ で状態 $\\rho_k$ に系が準備される場合、得られる状態は次の密度行列で表されます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a *convex combination* of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1}$.\n"
msgstr "これが密度行列 $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1}$ の*凸結合*です。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It follows that if we have $m$ quantum state vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{m-1}\\rangle$, and we prepare a system in the state $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ with probability $p_k$ for each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, the state we obtain is represented by the density matrix\n"
msgstr "$m$ 個の量子状態ベクトル $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{m-1}\\rangle$ があり、各 $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ に対して確率 $p_k$ で系を状態 $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ に準備するとき、得られる状態は次の密度行列で表されます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, if a qubit is prepared in the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and in the state $\\vert + \\rangle$ with probability $1/2$, the density matrix representation of the state we obtain is given by\n"
msgstr "例えば、量子ビットを確率 $1/2$ で状態 $\\vert 0\\rangle$ に、確率 $1/2$ で状態 $\\vert + \\rangle$ に準備するとき、得られる状態の密度行列表現は次のようになります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm] \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the simplified formulation of quantum information, averaging quantum state vectors like this doesn't work.\n"
"For instance, the vector\n"
msgstr ""
"量子情報の簡略的な定式化では、このように量子状態ベクトルを平均化することはできません。\n"
"例えば、次のベクトル\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\[1mm] 0\\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\[1mm] 0\\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is not a valid quantum state vector because its Euclidean norm is not equal to $1$.\n"
"A more extreme example that shows that this doesn't work for quantum state vectors is that we fix any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that we wish, and then we take our state to be $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and $-\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$.\n"
"These states differ by a global phase, so they're actually the same state — but averaging gives us the zero vector, which is not a valid quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"はユークリッドノルムが $1$ に等しくないため、有効な量子状態ベクトルではありません。\n"
"量子状態ベクトルでは機能しないことを示す、より極端な例として、任意の量子状態ベクトル $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ を選び、確率 $1/2$ でその状態を $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$、確率 $1/2$ で $-\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ とする場合を考えます。\n"
"これらの状態はグローバル位相だけ異なるため、実際には同じ状態ですが、平均をとるとゼロベクトルになり、これは有効な量子状態ベクトルではありません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The completely mixed state {#the-completely-mixed-state}"
msgstr "完全混合状態 {#the-completely-mixed-state}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose we set the state of a qubit to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$ or $\\vert 1\\rangle$ randomly, each with probability $1/2$.\n"
"The density matrix representing the resulting state is as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"量子ビットの状態を、それぞれ確率 $1/2$ でランダムに $\\vert 0\\rangle$ または $\\vert 1\\rangle$ に設定するとします。\n"
"得られる状態を表す密度行列は次のようになります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(In this equation the symbol $\\mathbb{I}$ denotes the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix.)\n"
"This is a special state known as the *completely mixed state*.\n"
"It represents complete uncertainty about the state of a qubit, similar to a uniform random bit in the probabilistic setting.\n"
msgstr ""
"（この式で $\\mathbb{I}$ は $2\\times 2$ の単位行列を表します。）\n"
"これは*完全混合状態*として知られる特別な状態です。\n"
"量子ビットの状態についての完全な不確かさを表し、確率的設定における一様ランダムビットに類似しています。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that we change the procedure: in place of the states $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$ we'll use the states $\\vert + \\rangle$ and $\\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"We can compute the density matrix that describes the resulting state in a similar way.\n"
msgstr ""
"ここで手続きを変えてみましょう。状態 $\\vert 0\\rangle$ と $\\vert 1\\rangle$ の代わりに、状態 $\\vert + \\rangle$ と $\\vert - \\rangle$ を使います。\n"
"同様の方法で、得られる状態を表す密度行列を計算できます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's the same density matrix as before, even though we changed the states.\n"
"In fact, we would again obtain the same result — the completely mixed state — by substituting *any* two orthogonal qubit state vectors for $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"状態を変えたにもかかわらず、密度行列は以前と同じです。\n"
"実際、$\\vert 0\\rangle$ と $\\vert 1\\rangle$ の代わりに*任意の* 2 つの直交する量子ビット状態ベクトルを代入しても、同じ結果、すなわち完全混合状態が得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a feature, not a bug!\n"
"We do in fact obtain exactly the same state either way.\n"
"That is, there's no way to distinguish the two procedures by measuring the qubit they produce, even in a statistical sense.\n"
"Our two different procedures are simply different ways to prepare this state.\n"
msgstr ""
"これは欠陥ではなく、特徴です！\n"
"実際、どちらの方法でも全く同じ状態が得られます。\n"
"つまり、2 つの手続きが生成する量子ビットを測定しても、統計的な意味でも両者を区別する方法はありません。\n"
"2 つの異なる手続きは、この状態を準備するための単に異なる方法に過ぎません。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can verify that this makes sense by thinking about what we could hope to learn given a random selection of a state from one of the two possible state sets $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$ and $\\{\\vert +\\rangle,\\vert -\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"To keep things simple, let's suppose that we perform a unitary operation $U$ on our qubit and then measure in the standard basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"2 つの可能な状態集合 $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$ と $\\{\\vert +\\rangle,\\vert -\\rangle\\}$ のいずれかからランダムに状態を選択したとき、何を学べるかを考えることで、これが意味をなすことを確認できます。\n"
"簡単のために、量子ビットにユニタリ演算 $U$ を施してから標準基底で測定するとします。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the first scenario, the state of the qubit is chosen uniformly from the set $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"If the state is $\\vert 0\\rangle$, we obtain the outcomes $0$ and $1$ with probabilities\n"
msgstr ""
"最初のシナリオでは、量子ビットの状態は集合 $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$ から一様に選ばれます。\n"
"状態が $\\vert 0\\rangle$ の場合、結果 $0$ と $1$ はそれぞれ次の確率で得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"respectively.\n"
"If the state is $\\vert 1\\rangle$, we obtain the outcomes $0$ and $1$ with probabilities\n"
msgstr "状態が $\\vert 1\\rangle$ の場合、結果 $0$ と $1$ は次の確率で得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the two possibilities each happen with probability $1/2$, we obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr "2 つの可能性はそれぞれ確率 $1/2$ で起こるため、結果 $0$ が得られる確率は\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr "であり、結果 $1$ が得られる確率は\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both of these expressions are equal to $1/2$.\n"
"One way to argue this is to use a fact from linear algebra that can be seen as a generalization of the Pythagorean theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"これら2つの式はどちらも$1/2$に等しくなります。\n"
"これを議論する一つの方法は、ピタゴラスの定理の一般化とも見なせる線形代数の事実を利用することです。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Suppose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of a (real or complex) vector space $\\mathcal{V}$. For every vector $\\vert \\phi\\rangle \\in \\mathcal{V}$ we have\n"
"$\\vert \\langle \\psi_1\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\vert^2 + \\cdots + \\vert \\langle \\psi_n \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\vert^2 = \\| \\vert\\phi\\rangle \\|^2$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"定理\">\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$が（実または複素の）ベクトル空間$\\mathcal{V}$の正規直交基底であるとします。任意のベクトル$\\vert \\phi\\rangle \\in \\mathcal{V}$に対して\n"
"$\\vert \\langle \\psi_1\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\vert^2 + \\cdots + \\vert \\langle \\psi_n \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\vert^2 = \\| \\vert\\phi\\rangle \\|^2$が成り立ちます。\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can apply this theorem to determine the probabilities as follows.\n"
"The probability to get $0$ is\n"
msgstr ""
"この定理を適用して、確率を次のように求めることができます。\n"
"$0$を得る確率は\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the probability to get $1$ is\n"
msgstr "そして$1$を得る確率は\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\Bigl(\n"
"\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"\\Bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $U$ is unitary, we know that $U^{\\dagger}$ is unitary as well, implying that both $U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle$ and $U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle$ are unit vectors.\n"
"Both probabilities are therefore equal to $1/2$.\n"
"This means that no matter how we choose $U$, we're just going to get a uniform random bit from the measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"$U$ はユニタリなので $U^{\\dagger}$ もユニタリであり、$U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle$ と $U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle$ はいずれも単位ベクトルです。\n"
"したがって、どちらの確率も $1/2$ に等しくなります。\n"
"つまり、$U$ をどのように選んでも、測定からは一様ランダムなビットが得られるだけです。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can perform a similar verification for any other pair of orthonormal states in place of $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"For example, because $\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis, the probability to obtain the measurement outcome $0$ in the second procedure is\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\vert 0\\rangle$ と $\\vert 1\\rangle$ の代わりに任意の 2 つの正規直交状態に対しても、同様の検証ができます。\n"
"例えば、$\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$ は正規直交基底であるため、第 2 の手続きで測定結果 $0$ が得られる確率は\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert + \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert - \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert + \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 0 \\vert U \\vert - \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert + \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert - \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert + \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2}\\vert \\langle 1 \\vert U \\vert - \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl\\| U^{\\dagger} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, we obtain exactly the same output statistics as we did for the states $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "特に、状態 $\\vert 0\\rangle$ と $\\vert 1\\rangle$ の場合と全く同じ出力統計が得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic states {#probabilistic-states}"
msgstr "確率的状態 {#probabilistic-states}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical states can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"In particular, for each classical state $a$ of a system $\\mathsf{X}$, the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"古典的状態は密度行列で表すことができます。\n"
"特に、系 $\\mathsf{X}$ の各古典的状態 $a$ に対して、密度行列\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"represents $\\mathsf{X}$ being definitively in the classical state $a$.\n"
"For qubits we have\n"
msgstr ""
"は $\\mathsf{X}$ が古典的状態 $a$ に確定的にあることを表します。\n"
"量子ビットの場合、\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and in general we have a single $1$ on the diagonal in the position corresponding to the classical state we have in mind, with all other entries zero.\n"
msgstr "であり、一般的には、対象とする古典的状態に対応する対角位置に $1$ が 1 つあり、他のすべての要素はゼロです。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can then take convex combinations of these density matrices to represent probabilistic states.\n"
"Supposing for simplicity that our classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, if  $\\mathsf{X}$ is in the state $a$ with probability $p_a$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, then the density matrix we obtain is\n"
msgstr ""
"これらの密度行列の凸結合をとることで、確率的状態を表すことができます。\n"
"簡単のために古典的状態集合を $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ とし、各 $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ に対して $\\mathsf{X}$ が確率 $p_a$ で状態 $a$ にあるとき、得られる密度行列は\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"p_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & p_1 & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\ddots & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & \\cdots & 0 & p_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"p_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & p_1 & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\ddots & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & \\cdots & 0 & p_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Going in the other direction, any diagonal density matrix can naturally be identified with the probabilistic state we obtain by simply reading the probability vector off from the diagonal.\n"
msgstr "逆方向に考えると、任意の対角密度行列は、対角から確率ベクトルを読み取るだけで、自然に確率的状態と対応付けられます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To be clear, when a density matrix is diagonal, it's not necessarily the case that we're talking about a classical system, or that the system must have been prepared through the random selection of a classical state, but rather that the state *could* have been obtained through the random selection of a classical state.\n"
msgstr "明確にしておくと、密度行列が対角であるとき、それは必ずしも古典的システムを扱っていることや、系が古典的状態のランダム選択によって準備されたことを意味するわけではありません。むしろ、状態が古典的状態のランダム選択によって*得られた可能性がある*ということです。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that probabilistic states are represented by diagonal density matrices is consistent with the intuition suggested at the start of the lesson that off-diagonal entries describe the degree to which the two classical states corresponding to the row and column of that entry are in quantum superposition.\n"
"Here, all of the off-diagonal entries are zero, so we just have classical randomness and nothing is in quantum superposition.\n"
msgstr ""
"確率的状態が対角密度行列で表されるという事実は、このレッスンの冒頭で示唆された直感、すなわち非対角要素がその行と列に対応する 2 つの古典的状態が量子重ね合わせにある程度を表すという直感と一致しています。\n"
"ここでは非対角要素がすべてゼロなので、古典的ランダム性のみがあり、量子重ね合わせは存在しません。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Density matrices and the spectral theorem {#density-matrices-and-the-spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "密度行列とスペクトル定理 {#density-matrices-and-the-spectral-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We've seen that if we take a convex combination of pure states,\n"
msgstr "純粋状態の凸結合を取ると、次のようになることを見てきました。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we obtain a density matrix.\n"
"Every density matrix $\\rho$, in fact, can be expressed as a convex combination of pure states like this.\n"
"That is, there will always exist a collection of unit vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ and a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1})$ for which the equation above is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"をとると、密度行列が得られることを見てきました。\n"
"実はすべての密度行列 $\\rho$ は、このような純粋状態の凸結合として表すことができます。\n"
"すなわち、上の等式が成り立つような単位ベクトルの集合 $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ と確率ベクトル $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1})$ が常に存在します。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can, moreover, always choose the number $m$ so that it agrees with the number of classical states of the system being considered, and we can select the quantum state vectors to be orthogonal.\n"
"The spectral theorem, which we encountered in the \"Foundations of quantum algorithms\" course, allows us to conclude this.\n"
"Here's a restatement of the spectral theorem for convenience.\n"
msgstr ""
"さらに、考えている系の古典的状態の数と一致するように $m$ を選び、量子状態ベクトルが直交するように選ぶことが常にできます。\n"
"「量子アルゴリズムの基礎」コースで学んだスペクトル定理により、このことが分かります。\n"
"参考のためにスペクトル定理を再掲します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a *normal* $n\\times n$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $n$ dimensional complex vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{n-1}\\rangle \\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1}$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"定理\">\n"
"スペクトル定理: $M$ を*正規*な $n\\times n$ 複素行列とします。\n"
"$n$ 次元複素ベクトルの正規直交基底 $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{n-1}\\rangle \\}$ と複素数 $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1}$ が存在して、次が成り立ちます。\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Recall that a matrix $M$ is *normal* if it satisfies $M^{\\dagger} M = M M^{\\dagger}$. In words, normal matrices are matrices that commute with their own conjugate transpose.)\n"
msgstr "（行列 $M$ が $M^{\\dagger} M = M M^{\\dagger}$ を満たすとき、$M$ は*正規*であると言います。言葉で言えば、正規行列とは自身の共役転置と交換可能な行列です。）\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can apply the spectral theorem to any given density matrix $\\rho$ because density matrices are always Hermitian and therefore normal.\n"
"This allows us to write\n"
msgstr ""
"密度行列は常にエルミートであり、したがって正規であるため、スペクトル定理を任意の密度行列 $\\rho$ に適用することができます。\n"
"これにより、ある正規直交基底 $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ に対して\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some orthonormal basis $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"It remains to verify that $(\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1})$ is a probability vector, which we can then rename to $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ if we wish.\n"
msgstr ""
"と書けます。\n"
"$(\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1})$ が確率ベクトルであることを確認する必要がありますが、確認できれば $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ と名前を変えることができます。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The numbers $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $\\rho$, and because $\\rho$ is positive semidefinite, these numbers must therefore be nonnegative real numbers.\n"
"We can conclude that $\\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} = 1$ from the fact that $\\rho$ has trace equal to $1$.\n"
"Going through the details will give us an opportunity to point out the following important and very useful property of the trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"数 $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1}$ は $\\rho$ の固有値であり、$\\rho$ が半正定値であるため、これらは非負の実数でなければなりません。\n"
"$\\rho$ のトレースが $1$ に等しいことから、$\\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} = 1$ が分かります。\n"
"詳細を確認することで、トレースの次の重要で非常に有用な性質を指摘する機会が得られます。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Cyclic property of the trace: For any two matrices $A$ and $B$ that give us a square matrix $AB$ by multiplying, the equality $\\operatorname{Tr}(AB) = \\operatorname{Tr}(BA)$ is true.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"定理\">\n"
"トレースの巡回性：正方行列 $AB$ を与える 2 つの行列 $A$ と $B$ に対して、$\\operatorname{Tr}(AB) = \\operatorname{Tr}(BA)$ が成り立ちます。\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this theorem works even if $A$ and $B$ are not themselves square matrices.\n"
"That is, we may have that $A$ is $n\\times m$ and $B$ is $m\\times n$, for some choice of positive integers $n$ and $m$, so that $AB$ is an $n\\times n$ square matrix and $BA$ is $m\\times m$.\n"
msgstr ""
"この定理は $A$ と $B$ が正方行列でなくても成り立ちます。\n"
"つまり、正の整数 $n$ と $m$ に対して、$A$ が $n\\times m$、$B$ が $m\\times n$ であっても構いません。この場合、$AB$ は $n\\times n$ の正方行列、$BA$ は $m\\times m$ の正方行列になります。\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, if we let $A$ be a column vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ and let $B$ be the row vector $\\langle \\phi\\vert$, then we see that\n"
msgstr "特に、$A$ を列ベクトル $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$、$B$ を行ベクトル $\\langle \\phi\\vert$ とすると、\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\bigr) = \\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\bigr) = \\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second equality follows from the fact that $\\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ is a scalar, which we can also think of as a $1\\times 1$ matrix whose trace is its single entry.\n"
"Using this fact, we can conclude that $\\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} = 1$ by the linearity of the trace function.\n"
msgstr ""
"2番目の等式は、$\\langle\\phi\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ がスカラーであり、これはトレースがその単一の要素であるような $1\\times 1$ 行列とも考えられるという事実から導かれます。\n"
"この事実を使うと、トレース関数の線形性により $\\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} = 1$ であると結論できます。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"1 = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"= \\lambda_0 \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert\\bigr) + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"1 = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\lambda_0 \\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"= \\lambda_0 \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_0\\rangle\\langle \\psi_0\\vert\\bigr) + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{n-1}\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{n-1}\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\lambda_0 + \\cdots + \\lambda_{n-1}\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, we can reach the same conclusion by using the fact that the trace of a square matrix (even one that isn't normal) is equal to the sum of its eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr "別の方法として、正方行列(正規でないものも含む)のトレースはその固有値の和に等しいという事実を使って、同じ結論に到達することもできます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We have therefore concluded that any given density matrix $\\rho$ can be expressed as a convex combination of pure states.\n"
"We also see that we can, moreover, take the pure states to be *orthogonal*.\n"
"This means, in particular, that we never need the number $n$ to be larger than the size of the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"したがって、任意の与えられた密度行列 $\\rho$ は純粋状態の凸結合として表せることが分かりました。\n"
"さらに、その純粋状態を*直交*するものとして取れることも分かります。\n"
"これは特に、数 $n$ を $\\mathsf{X}$ の古典状態集合のサイズより大きくする必要が決してないことを意味します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, it must be understood that there will be different ways to write a density matrix as a convex combination of pure states, not just the ways that the spectral theorem provides.\n"
"A previous example illustrates this.\n"
msgstr ""
"一般に、密度行列を純粋状態の凸結合として書く方法は、スペクトル定理が提供する方法だけでなく、他にもさまざまな方法があることを理解しておく必要があります。\n"
"前の例がこれを示しています。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is not a spectral decomposition of this matrix because $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert + \\rangle$ are not orthogonal.\n"
"Here's a spectral decomposition:\n"
msgstr ""
"これはこの行列のスペクトル分解ではありません。なぜなら $\\vert 0\\rangle$ と $\\vert + \\rangle$ は直交していないからです。\n"
"ここにスペクトル分解を示します。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"The eigenvalues are numbers that will likely look familiar:\n"
msgstr ""
"ここで $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle$ です。\n"
"固有値はおそらく見覚えのある数になります。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85 \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\sin^2(\\pi/8) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.15.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85 \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\sin^2(\\pi/8) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.15.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The eigenvectors can be written explicitly like this.\n"
msgstr "固有ベクトルはこのように明示的に書くことができます。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & =\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & =\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & =\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & =\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As another, more general example, suppose $\\vert \\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\phi_{99} \\rangle$ are quantum state vectors representing states of a single qubit, chosen arbitrarily — so we're not assuming any particular relationships among these vectors.\n"
"We could then consider the state we obtain by choosing one of these $100$ states uniformly at random:\n"
msgstr ""
"別のより一般的な例として、$\\vert \\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\phi_{99} \\rangle$ が単一のキュビットの状態を表す量子状態ベクトルであり、任意に選ばれているとしましょう — つまり、これらのベクトル間に特定の関係を仮定していません。\n"
"これら $100$ 個の状態の1つを一様ランダムに選ぶことで得られる状態を考えることができます。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{100} \\sum_{k = 0}^{99} \\vert \\phi_k\\rangle\\langle \\phi_k \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{100} \\sum_{k = 0}^{99} \\vert \\phi_k\\rangle\\langle \\phi_k \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we're talking about a qubit, the density matrix $\\rho$ is $2\\times 2$, so by the spectral theorem we could alternatively write\n"
msgstr "キュビットについて話しているので、密度行列 $\\rho$ は $2\\times 2$ です。したがって、スペクトル定理により、代わりに次のように書くこともできます。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = p \\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert + (1 - p) \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = p \\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert + (1 - p) \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for some real number $p\\in[0,1]$ and an orthonormal basis $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\}$ — but naturally the existence of this expression doesn't prohibit us from writing $\\rho$ as an average of 100 pure states if we choose to do that.\n"
msgstr "ある実数 $p\\in[0,1]$ と正規直交基底 $\\{\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\}$ に対して — ただし、この表現が存在するからといって、$\\rho$ を 100 個の純粋状態の平均として書くことを選んでも構わないことに変わりはありません。\n"
